            <title>[LU-21327] rustreapi: add a safe data version API</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21327</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Add &lt;tt&gt;rustreapi::data_version()&lt;/tt&gt;, a safe wrapper for &lt;tt&gt;llapi_get_data_version()&lt;/tt&gt; / &lt;tt&gt;LL_IOC_DATA_VERSION&lt;/tt&gt;.  It takes a &lt;tt&gt;BorrowedFd&lt;/tt&gt; and a &lt;tt&gt;DataVersionFlags&lt;/tt&gt; bitflags set, and returns the file's &lt;tt&gt;u64&lt;/tt&gt; data version.  The flags are &lt;tt&gt;ReadFlush&lt;/tt&gt; (&lt;tt&gt;LL_DV_RD_FLUSH&lt;/tt&gt;) and &lt;tt&gt;WriteFlush&lt;/tt&gt; (&lt;tt&gt;LL_DV_WR_FLUSH&lt;/tt&gt;).  &lt;tt&gt;DataVersionError&lt;/tt&gt; gives separate variants for:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;a descriptor that is not a regular file on Lustre (&lt;tt&gt;ENOTTY&lt;/tt&gt;, which includes a Lustre directory);&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;an &lt;tt&gt;O_PATH&lt;/tt&gt; descriptor (&lt;tt&gt;EBADF&lt;/tt&gt;);&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;any other errno.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Each call is a single ioctl, with no open, stat or allocation.  That makes it cheap enough to call on every request.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;LL_DV_SZ_UPDATE&lt;/tt&gt; is not exposed: &lt;tt&gt;ll_file_ioctl()&lt;/tt&gt; masks it off &lt;tt&gt;LL_IOC_DATA_VERSION&lt;/tt&gt;, so it has no effect from user space.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The change includes unit tests and a &lt;tt&gt;data_version_test&lt;/tt&gt; integration test, which &lt;tt&gt;rustreapi-test.sh&lt;/tt&gt; runs.  It depends on &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21329" title="rustreapi: build fails against 2.17.50-2.17.58 headers (volatile calls gated on LUSTRE_2_18)" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-21329"&gt;LU-21329&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20663" title="rustreapi: lsp_stripe_pattern union breaks build against master lustreapi.h" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20663"&gt;LU-20663&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
